    {
      "text": "When Mankey starts shaking and its nasal breathing turns rough, it’s a sure sign that it is becoming angry. However, because it goes into a towering rage almost instantly, it is impossible for anyone to flee its wrath.",
      "version": "omega-ruby"
    },
    {
      "text": "When Mankey starts shaking and its nasal breathing turns rough, it’s a sure sign that it is becoming angry. However, because it goes into a towering rage almost instantly, it is impossible for anyone to flee its wrath.",
      "version": "alpha-sapphire"
    },
    {
      "text": "It can spontaneously become enraged. Everyone near it clears out as it rampages, and the resulting loneliness makes it angrier still.",
      "version": "sun"
    },
    {
      "text": "Its raging tires it out and causes it to fall asleep, but the anger resonating in its dreams causes it to wake up—which infuriates it all over again.",
      "version": "moon"
    },
    {
      "text": "The smallest of things could cause it to lose its temper. Because it doesn’t hold in its stress, this Pokémon can live a long time.",
      "version": "ultra-sun"
    },
    {
      "text": "If one gets angry, all the others around it will get angry, so silence is a rare visitor in a troop of Mankey.",
      "version": "ultra-moon"
    },
    {
      "text": "An agile Pokémon that lives in trees. It angers easily and will not hesitate to attack anything.",
